    "body": "## Superseded by the #969 mechanism-first pivot\n\nThis issue is closed as `not planned` and has no native blocker role. Its proposed repair scope was absorbed directly into #969 before any #974 implementation or evidence was collected.\n\nPR #975 was closed without merge. The historical #969 capacity census remains useful defect evidence, but it no longer closes #969. Active work stays in #969 until one exact non-H4 ordered transport, one frozen selector, the matched 2–8-unit decoded Gate 0, and independent sentence qualification reach `PROMOTE_LOCAL_SENTENCE_CONSUMER_TO_I1`.\n\n## Preserved hypothesis\n\nThe absorbed hypothesis is:\n\n- exact associative, noncommutative transported-path composition in real non-digest state;\n- a candidate-relative interaction that does not cancel or merely append history;\n- a causal lexical return-memory analogue computed only from past/current state;\n- selective promotion to richer ordered state when a smaller chart aliases candidates;\n- optional typed factor/semiprime/divisibility transport only with public units and inverse/error contracts; and\n- exact finite-table or integer lowering.\n\n#969 owns implementation and evidence. #953 and #973 remain blocked by #969. This closed issue is historical programme provenance, not a completed mechanism or a future work item.",
